WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.276 --> 00:00:01.446
- And you're lookin' up at me, and said,

00:00:01.446 --> 00:00:03.083
Ali, don't do it!

00:00:03.083 --> 00:00:03.956
I'm choppin' trees.

00:00:03.956 --> 00:00:05.555
I've done somethin' special.

00:00:05.555 --> 00:00:07.515
Now, don't pay no attention
to what they say about me.

00:00:07.515 --> 00:00:10.633
I told you all, that I was
the greatest of all time!

00:00:10.633 --> 00:00:13.752
But, my main fight is
for freedom and equality.

00:00:13.752 --> 00:00:15.360
You really can't plan a fight,

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.731
when you're meetin' a man
you never met before, right?

00:00:17.731 --> 00:00:19.293
I'm going to dance and be pretty.

00:00:19.293 --> 00:00:20.602
I'm just gon' win on points.

00:00:20.602 --> 00:00:23.710
Maybe, sometimes, the
wheel can outdo the skill.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.587
You are fightin' the greatest
fighter of all times!

00:00:26.587 --> 00:00:28.665
This is the Ali Shuffle!

00:00:28.665 --> 00:00:31.120
(audience cheering)

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.741
- He's an American former
professional boxer.

00:00:33.741 --> 00:00:36.379
He's widely considered among
the greatest heavyweights

00:00:36.379 --> 00:00:37.999
in the history of the sport.

00:00:37.999 --> 00:00:40.118
He's one of the most
recognized sports figures

00:00:40.118 --> 00:00:41.941
of the past hundred years.

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:43.131
He's Muhammad Ali,

00:00:43.131 --> 00:00:46.714
and here are his Top
Ten Rules for Success.

00:00:49.012 --> 00:00:51.841
- My thinkin' is so superior,

00:00:51.841 --> 00:00:53.638
and my knowledge is so positive,

00:00:53.638 --> 00:00:56.026
and my logic is so wise,

00:00:56.026 --> 00:01:00.477
until it clashes with the
mentality, which is down here,

00:01:00.477 --> 00:01:02.376
and I'm over there.
(audience laughing)

00:01:02.376 --> 00:01:05.172
So, me bein' so high, I can see more,

00:01:05.172 --> 00:01:07.145
and see farther than you.

00:01:07.145 --> 00:01:09.806
And you're lookin' up at me,
and said, Ali, don't do it!

00:01:09.806 --> 00:01:11.498
(audience laughing)

00:01:11.498 --> 00:01:14.616
Ali, please stop makin' it hurt!

00:01:14.616 --> 00:01:18.328
And you're on the job,
makin' 60, 70 pounds a week,

00:01:18.328 --> 00:01:20.586
on whoever this guy is.
(audience laughing)

00:01:20.586 --> 00:01:22.925
Never been out of the country.

00:01:22.925 --> 00:01:25.227
Not known in his own neighborhood.

00:01:25.227 --> 00:01:26.789
Ali, don't do it!

00:01:26.789 --> 00:01:29.703
But, I'm at such a high level,
until I don't think like you.

00:01:29.703 --> 00:01:31.171
I'm not like you.

00:01:31.171 --> 00:01:34.750
I'm not, so you, and
me, and another person.

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:36.596
- But, you know why they say that?

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:38.500
It makes for the best possible reasons.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.412
- They fear and they are wary.

00:01:40.412 --> 00:01:41.849
It looks dangerous to them.

00:01:41.849 --> 00:01:43.997
And it's not really that dangerous to me.

00:01:43.997 --> 00:01:48.164
(audience roaring)
(upbeat music)

00:01:49.967 --> 00:01:51.511
- [Announcer] A little
more than halfway through.

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:53.344
He's being aggressive!

00:02:01.475 --> 00:02:02.308
Down!

00:02:03.716 --> 00:02:07.883
He was knocked down, clearly
with a straight right!

00:02:28.213 --> 00:02:29.046
- No problem!

00:02:29.046 --> 00:02:32.686
This will be the biggest
upset since Sonny Liston.

00:02:32.686 --> 00:02:34.714
And I think it is befittin',

00:02:34.714 --> 00:02:37.675
that I go out of boxing,
just like I came in,

00:02:37.675 --> 00:02:42.185
defeatin' a big, bad monster
that nobody could destroy!

00:02:42.185 --> 00:02:43.966
A hard punch!

00:02:43.966 --> 00:02:45.500
I'm the underdog!

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.641
If he hits me, I'm in trouble,
like the Sonnny Liston fight!

00:02:48.641 --> 00:02:52.411
But, I came back, and I shook
the world, and I got Liston.

00:02:52.411 --> 00:02:54.472
Now, it's ten years since Sonny Liston.

00:02:54.472 --> 00:02:57.781
I'm meetin' another big,
bad, strong monster,

00:02:57.781 --> 00:02:59.934
knockout artist, that beats everybody!

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:02.413
Sonny Liston knocked out Patterson twice!

00:03:02.413 --> 00:03:04.256
And I was supposed to fall!

00:03:04.256 --> 00:03:06.123
But, he didn't knock me out.

00:03:06.123 --> 00:03:08.656
Because he could hit hard,

00:03:08.656 --> 00:03:10.481
but he couldn't find nothin' to hit.

00:03:10.481 --> 00:03:12.583
George Foreman knocked out Ken Norton,

00:03:12.583 --> 00:03:14.545
knocked out Joe Frazier.

00:03:14.545 --> 00:03:15.964
True, I didn't knock 'em out.

00:03:15.964 --> 00:03:17.172
But, I'm so fast.

00:03:17.172 --> 00:03:18.005
I'm so hard to hit.

00:03:18.005 --> 00:03:19.168
I'm so scientific.

00:03:19.168 --> 00:03:21.879
I'm a totally different man,
from Frazier and Norton.

00:03:21.879 --> 00:03:22.817
Listen, David.

00:03:22.817 --> 00:03:24.126
When I meet this man,

00:03:24.126 --> 00:03:28.041
if you think the world was
surprised when Nixon resigned,

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:30.050
wait 'til I whip Foreman's behind!

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:34.938
(audience laughing and clapping)

00:03:34.938 --> 00:03:35.927
I'm tellin' ya, David.

00:03:35.927 --> 00:03:39.265
I'm down to 215 pounds, right now.

00:03:39.265 --> 00:03:42.394
I said it, when 215, I'm
fightin' weight already!

00:03:42.394 --> 00:03:44.347
I usually train six weeks for a fight!

00:03:44.347 --> 00:03:45.955
I've trained four months for a fight!

00:03:45.955 --> 00:03:47.098
I'm choppin' trees!

00:03:47.098 --> 00:03:48.770
I've done somethin' special.

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:50.726
I've wrestled with a alligator.

00:03:50.726 --> 00:03:52.634
(audience laughing)

00:03:52.634 --> 00:03:53.890
- [David] I believe you totally!

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:54.868
I believe you completely!

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:56.987
- I have tussled with a whale!

00:03:56.987 --> 00:03:58.655
I done handcuffed lightnin'.

00:03:58.655 --> 00:04:00.353
Throw thunder in jail!

00:04:00.353 --> 00:04:01.404
Now, you know I'm bad!

00:04:01.404 --> 00:04:04.936
Only last week, I murdered
a rock, injured a stone,

00:04:04.936 --> 00:04:06.756
hospitalized a brick!

00:04:06.756 --> 00:04:08.953
I'm so mean, I make medicine sick!

00:04:08.953 --> 00:04:12.941
(David and audience laughing)
The man's in trouble!

00:04:12.941 --> 00:04:13.774
Listen!

00:04:13.774 --> 00:04:16.714
George Foreman, people are
afraid of George Foreman!

00:04:16.714 --> 00:04:18.424
They talk about how hard he hits!

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:21.259
The world has been deceived,
you listen to me now!

00:04:21.259 --> 00:04:22.467
I've never told you wrong!

00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:24.136
The man don't hit hard!

00:04:24.136 --> 00:04:26.376
He knocked Joe Frazier down six times!

00:04:26.376 --> 00:04:27.976
He got up six times!

00:04:27.976 --> 00:04:30.576
Joe King Roman, his Tokyo, Japan fight,

00:04:30.576 --> 00:04:32.106
the Puerto Rican champion!

00:04:32.106 --> 00:04:33.419
Knocked him down three times!

00:04:33.419 --> 00:04:35.124
He jumped up three times!

00:04:35.124 --> 00:04:37.313
He knocked Ken Norton down four times!

00:04:37.313 --> 00:04:38.723
He jumped up four times!

00:04:38.723 --> 00:04:40.250
When have you ever saw the man say,

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:43.304
seven, eight, nine,
ten, count his man out?

00:04:43.304 --> 00:04:45.272
When I hit Sonny Liston the second fight,

00:04:45.272 --> 00:04:47.051
he stayed out for the count of ten!

00:04:47.051 --> 00:04:49.565
Zora Folley stayed out
for the count of ten!

00:04:49.565 --> 00:04:51.844
Cleveland Williams stayed
out for the count of ten!

00:04:51.844 --> 00:04:53.974
What few I have knocked out, stayed down!

00:04:53.974 --> 00:04:56.676
Sugar Ray Robinson, knocked
him out for the count of 30!

00:04:56.676 --> 00:04:59.686
Joe Louis, Marciano, Jack
Dempsey, Jack Johnson,

00:04:59.686 --> 00:05:01.125
Archie Moore, Ezzard Charles!

00:05:01.125 --> 00:05:02.757
They knock 'em out cold!

00:05:02.757 --> 00:05:05.586
So, this man has never
knocked nobody out cold!

00:05:05.586 --> 00:05:06.579
He's a bully!

00:05:06.579 --> 00:05:07.412
He's slow!

00:05:07.412 --> 00:05:10.010
He has no skill, no
footwork, he's awkward!

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:12.291
And I have even given him a name.

00:05:12.291 --> 00:05:14.024
I named Floyd Patterson The Rabbit.

00:05:14.024 --> 00:05:16.073
I named Sunny Liston The Bear.

00:05:16.073 --> 00:05:19.661
And he shall be known as,
officially, as The Mummy!

00:05:19.661 --> 00:05:20.871
(audience laughing)

00:05:20.871 --> 00:05:21.704
The Mummy!

00:05:23.759 --> 00:05:24.969
- [David] Why The Mummy?

00:05:24.969 --> 00:05:26.838
- Because he fights, when he fightin',

00:05:26.838 --> 00:05:28.510
if you ever watch him in the ring,

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:31.648
(stammers) he drags, like
that, after his opponent.

00:05:31.648 --> 00:05:35.481
(David and audience laughing)

00:05:36.858 --> 00:05:39.557
And how is a mummy going to catch me?

00:05:39.557 --> 00:05:40.666
When you're fightin' a mummy,

00:05:40.666 --> 00:05:42.674
you just keep a step ahead of the mummy!

00:05:42.674 --> 00:05:43.507
See?

00:05:43.507 --> 00:05:44.633
Yeah, just move on the mummy!

00:05:44.633 --> 00:05:45.835
No, mummy, I'm over here!

00:05:45.835 --> 00:05:47.397
No, mummy, I'm over here!

00:05:47.397 --> 00:05:48.877
Yeah, no, you're movin' too fast!

00:05:48.877 --> 00:05:50.029
The mummy don't move that fast!

00:05:50.029 --> 00:05:54.196
(audience laughing)
(upbeat music)

00:06:30.567 --> 00:06:32.709
I don't pay no attention
to what they say about me.

00:06:32.709 --> 00:06:35.110
All I do, is just do what I have to do,

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:37.179
and get paid, and that's it.

00:06:37.179 --> 00:06:38.741
But, I don't really pay no attention

00:06:38.741 --> 00:06:40.372
to the rules of boxing.

00:06:40.372 --> 00:06:41.272
I don't pay no attention.

00:06:41.272 --> 00:06:43.033
I defy all the rules.

00:06:43.033 --> 00:06:45.217
I've added pages to the book of boxing.

00:06:45.217 --> 00:06:47.601
I have this game to such a thing now,

00:06:47.601 --> 00:06:50.628
until boxing promoters can
no longer afford my shows.

00:06:50.628 --> 00:06:52.538
I have governments, like Iran,

00:06:52.538 --> 00:06:55.554
ready to put up ten million,
for me to fight Joe Frazier.

00:06:55.554 --> 00:06:57.846
I have governments, like Cairo, Egypt,

00:06:57.846 --> 00:07:00.505
wantin' to put up six million
with people like Ron Lyle.

00:07:00.505 --> 00:07:04.002
I have countries, all like,
all back throughout Zaire,

00:07:04.002 --> 00:07:05.076
talkin' to Mobuto.

00:07:05.076 --> 00:07:05.989
He wants 'em back again.

00:07:05.989 --> 00:07:09.502
They'll put up five more
million for a turn with Foreman.

00:07:09.502 --> 00:07:12.509
When we talk about ten
million, and six million,

00:07:12.509 --> 00:07:14.395
and four million, this is unbelievable!

00:07:14.395 --> 00:07:15.981
And they don't expect
to get the money back.

00:07:15.981 --> 00:07:18.010
They're promotin' their
countries and ideals.

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:20.950
So, I've like sales so,
in this sport of boxing,

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:23.559
until Madison Square Garden is too small.

00:07:23.559 --> 00:07:25.370
Yankee Stadium is too small.

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:26.767
The Houston Astrodome.

00:07:26.767 --> 00:07:29.387
The biggest promoters, and
the wealthiest Americans,

00:07:29.387 --> 00:07:31.707
and Englishmen, you
can get for promotions,

00:07:31.707 --> 00:07:33.706
cannot just promote me no more!

00:07:33.706 --> 00:07:34.539
You understand?

00:07:34.539 --> 00:07:37.007
So, I've not only added pages to boxing,

00:07:37.007 --> 00:07:40.257
but added new sections to the boxing book!

00:07:40.257 --> 00:07:42.840
(upbeat music)

00:07:51.005 --> 00:07:53.885
- [Announcer] We're now
well in the challenge...

00:07:53.885 --> 00:07:55.362
(audience cheering)

00:07:55.362 --> 00:07:57.445
And there, Folley's down!

00:07:59.273 --> 00:08:01.773
Five, six, seven, eight, nine!

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:07.880
Folley is up at nine!

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:09.846
Talk about Folley, right?

00:08:09.846 --> 00:08:11.372
He can't be in there, fighting himself.

00:08:11.372 --> 00:08:13.955
There's no question about that.

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:15.957
Folley's down!

00:08:17.539 --> 00:08:19.863
I don't know if he's
going to make this one!

00:08:19.863 --> 00:08:21.863
Six, seven, eight, nine!

00:08:24.843 --> 00:08:28.533
Nope, he can't really try to get up!

00:08:28.533 --> 00:08:33.483
And Muhammad Ali has been
named the heavyweight champion!

00:08:33.483 --> 00:08:37.146
- And everybody stop
talkin' now, attention!

00:08:37.146 --> 00:08:38.647
I told you!

00:08:38.647 --> 00:08:40.229
All of my critics!

00:08:40.229 --> 00:08:43.648
I told you all, that I was
the greatest of all time,

00:08:43.648 --> 00:08:45.201
when I beat Sonny Liston!

00:08:45.201 --> 00:08:48.928
I told you today, I'm still
the greatest of all time!

00:08:48.928 --> 00:08:51.462
Never again, will defeat me!

00:08:51.462 --> 00:08:53.760
Never again, say that
I'm going to be defeated!

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:56.378
Never again, better make me the underdog,

00:08:56.378 --> 00:08:58.027
until I'm about 50 years old!

00:08:58.027 --> 00:08:59.127
Then, you might get me!

00:08:59.127 --> 00:09:00.349
But, I didn't dance!

00:09:00.349 --> 00:09:01.957
I didn't dance for a reason!

00:09:01.957 --> 00:09:04.119
I wanted to make him lose all his power!

00:09:04.119 --> 00:09:05.867
I kept tellin' him, he had no punch!

00:09:05.867 --> 00:09:06.731
He couldn't hit!

00:09:06.731 --> 00:09:08.098
He swingin' like a sissy!

00:09:08.098 --> 00:09:09.021
He's missin'!

00:09:09.021 --> 00:09:09.981
Let me see ya box!

00:09:09.981 --> 00:09:11.522
I hadn't started dancin' yet!

00:09:11.522 --> 00:09:13.214
You can't say my legs are gone!

00:09:13.214 --> 00:09:15.905
You can't say I was tired,
because what happened?

00:09:15.905 --> 00:09:17.705
I didn't dance from the second right on!

00:09:17.705 --> 00:09:18.996
I stayed on the ropes!

00:09:18.996 --> 00:09:21.077
When I stay on the ropes,
you think I'm doin' bad!

00:09:21.077 --> 00:09:24.001
But, I want all boxers to put
this in the page of boxing!

00:09:24.001 --> 00:09:26.688
Stayin' on ropes is a beautiful
thing, with a heavyweight,

00:09:26.688 --> 00:09:28.360
when you make him shoot his best shots,

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:29.587
and you know he's not hittin' ya!

00:09:29.587 --> 00:09:31.285
I would've gave George Foreman two rounds,

00:09:31.285 --> 00:09:33.857
of steady punchin', because
after that, he was mine!

00:09:33.857 --> 00:09:36.440
(upbeat music)

00:09:40.887 --> 00:09:45.054
(groovy music)
(crowd roaring)

00:09:48.246 --> 00:09:50.829
- [Announcer] Ellis is reeling!

00:09:54.391 --> 00:09:58.010
He looks defenseless on the ropes!

00:09:58.010 --> 00:09:59.409
The referee may be deciding

00:09:59.409 --> 00:10:00.799
whether he's going to stop the fight!

00:10:00.799 --> 00:10:02.882
He is stopping the fight!

00:10:04.689 --> 00:10:06.520
- I really care nothin' about boxing.

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:08.320
Boxing is a stepping stone,

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:11.402
just to introduce me to the audience.

00:10:11.402 --> 00:10:15.151
(stammers) Like, if I was
still in Louisville, Kentucky,

00:10:15.151 --> 00:10:17.747
and never was a boxer, I
might get killed next week,

00:10:17.747 --> 00:10:19.354
in some type of little freedom struggle,

00:10:19.354 --> 00:10:21.404
and you'd never read the news.

00:10:21.404 --> 00:10:25.571
But now, if I even say the
wrong thing, it makes news.

00:10:26.706 --> 00:10:30.143
So like, boxing is just to
introduce me to the struggle.

00:10:30.143 --> 00:10:33.190
Like, when I speak, I draw
people, in the States,

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:35.890
to draw my people, to
teach 'em various things,

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:38.284
which'll give 'em dignity,
pride, and self-help,

00:10:38.284 --> 00:10:41.249
and go for self, or help the
ghetto, and help the dope,

00:10:41.249 --> 00:10:42.967
prostitution problem.

00:10:42.967 --> 00:10:44.475
The juveniles.

00:10:44.475 --> 00:10:46.725
And I use my image to
help, or do all I can,

00:10:46.725 --> 00:10:48.803
to stop a lot of trouble
among our own people,

00:10:48.803 --> 00:10:50.251
fightin' and killin' each other.

00:10:50.251 --> 00:10:52.811
So, boxing is just going
to be another year.

00:10:52.811 --> 00:10:55.339
Though my main fight is
for freedom and equality.

00:10:55.339 --> 00:10:57.803
And this is what I plan to do in boxing.

00:10:57.803 --> 00:10:59.019
It's good for livelihood.

00:10:59.019 --> 00:11:02.240
But mainly, money don't
really mean nothin',

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:03.979
'cause I proved that
when I gave up the title,

00:11:03.979 --> 00:11:06.420
not knowin' if I'm comin'
back, or not, for four years.

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:07.979
And they let me back on my terms.

00:11:07.979 --> 00:11:09.659
I didn't deny nothin' I believed.

00:11:09.659 --> 00:11:11.180
I'm still the same everything.

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:14.280
So if, even today, if my title
hadn't been given back to me,

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:16.027
if I had gotten such in poverty,

00:11:16.027 --> 00:11:18.747
where I had to go find a
job, I would have did that.

00:11:18.747 --> 00:11:21.826
But, I made a good livin'
speakin' in colleges,

00:11:21.826 --> 00:11:23.515
'cause the war, I got unpopular.

00:11:23.515 --> 00:11:24.688
And so many black militants,

00:11:24.688 --> 00:11:26.467
who were tryin' to do all they could,

00:11:26.467 --> 00:11:28.827
and I was naturally right
in the middle of all of it,

00:11:28.827 --> 00:11:30.684
and represented, and that kept me alive!

00:11:30.684 --> 00:11:33.166
But, if I couldn't fight, I
would still not be fightin'.

00:11:33.166 --> 00:11:34.907
So, number one, comes freedom first,

00:11:34.907 --> 00:11:36.062
and my people, equality.

00:11:36.062 --> 00:11:39.072
And this is what I plan to
do, after I through fightin',

00:11:39.072 --> 00:11:40.471
workin' with nothin' but the people,

00:11:40.471 --> 00:11:42.439
the little people in
alleys, the wine-heads,

00:11:42.439 --> 00:11:44.386
the downtrodden people,
goin' out among 'em,

00:11:44.386 --> 00:11:46.623
and helpin' 'em with my image.

00:11:46.623 --> 00:11:49.790
(upbeat groovy music)

00:11:55.517 --> 00:11:59.517
- [Announcer] Led with a
left, and another left.

00:12:00.977 --> 00:12:05.144
Ali is doing damage now, and
Blin is taking a beating!

00:12:07.104 --> 00:12:08.462
Oh, that right hand!

00:12:08.462 --> 00:12:10.433
It's over, hand's right,
I think he nailed him!

00:12:10.433 --> 00:12:13.492
Blin against the ropes,
hanging on, and on the canvas!

00:12:13.492 --> 00:12:15.410
He is down, this could be it!

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:17.108
- You know, I'm sure Henry'll tell you

00:12:17.108 --> 00:12:20.016
any fighter that knows what's happenin',

00:12:20.016 --> 00:12:21.607
you really can't plan a fight,

00:12:21.607 --> 00:12:24.176
when you're meetin' a man
you've never met before, right?

00:12:24.176 --> 00:12:25.615
You just have to get your tools ready.

00:12:25.615 --> 00:12:27.220
Here's a car, it stops on the highway.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:28.988
They call the Triple-A, or whatever,

00:12:28.988 --> 00:12:30.630
and said, my car is broke down.

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:32.160
What it is, the lady, she
don't know what's wrong.

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:33.997
But, the man comes with all the tools,

00:12:33.997 --> 00:12:36.526
and he come equipped to handle
whatever the problem is.

00:12:36.526 --> 00:12:38.159
A astronaut goes into space.

00:12:38.159 --> 00:12:41.694
And he pretends that
somethin' happens to the ship,

00:12:41.694 --> 00:12:42.814
before he take off.

00:12:42.814 --> 00:12:44.234
He gets out and he works on it.

00:12:44.234 --> 00:12:45.546
He's not lookin' for somethin' to happen,

00:12:45.546 --> 00:12:46.776
but it might happen.

00:12:46.776 --> 00:12:49.415
So, I just had everything ready.

00:12:49.415 --> 00:12:52.293
Now, after the first round,

00:12:52.293 --> 00:12:53.895
and bein' here, able to talk professional,

00:12:53.895 --> 00:12:55.846
a man so great, had so many knockouts,

00:12:55.846 --> 00:12:57.776
never been defeated,
never been even scratched.

00:12:57.776 --> 00:12:59.427
I didn't know, really, how good he was.

00:12:59.427 --> 00:13:01.764
So, I had to come in,
actually a little nervous,

00:13:01.764 --> 00:13:03.244
and with everything ready.

00:13:03.244 --> 00:13:05.122
After one round of dancin',

00:13:05.122 --> 00:13:08.141
I'd found out that this would tire me out.

00:13:08.141 --> 00:13:09.876
So, I would have resort to ropes.

00:13:09.876 --> 00:13:12.265
I figured that out after the first round.

00:13:12.265 --> 00:13:14.024
So, I said, I'm going
to go to these ropes.

00:13:14.024 --> 00:13:15.774
And I'mma let this man
through everything he can,

00:13:15.774 --> 00:13:16.773
let him tire himself out.

00:13:16.773 --> 00:13:17.747
He might look like he's winnin'.

00:13:17.747 --> 00:13:19.541
And if he don't hurt me, I'mma stay here.

00:13:19.541 --> 00:13:22.342
But, if he should be
great as they say he is,

00:13:22.342 --> 00:13:24.394
if he hits as hard as they say he hit,

00:13:24.394 --> 00:13:25.770
when he hits you, it breaks your arm.

00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:27.485
He knocked out Joe
Frazier, I couldn't do it,

00:13:27.485 --> 00:13:28.507
knocked out Ken Norton.

00:13:28.507 --> 00:13:31.067
He was a big, bad jabber
for the fight, you remember.

00:13:31.067 --> 00:13:32.235
And now, you remember that, don't ya?

00:13:32.235 --> 00:13:34.345
How bad he was?
(Dickie and audience laughing)

00:13:34.345 --> 00:13:35.184
They don't say that now,

00:13:35.184 --> 00:13:37.434
but you remember he was a real
bad catch of the day, right?

00:13:37.434 --> 00:13:38.386
Don't forget that.

00:13:38.386 --> 00:13:42.685
Now, after I found out he
didn't have it, I stayed there.

00:13:42.685 --> 00:13:44.966
But, if he had had what
I thought he had had,

00:13:44.966 --> 00:13:46.194
or what they say that he had,

00:13:46.194 --> 00:13:49.235
I'da kept runnin', hopin'
I wouldn't get tired.

00:13:49.235 --> 00:13:52.318
(upbeat funky music)

00:13:56.405 --> 00:13:57.914
- [Announcer] Jokin'
around from Muhammad Ali.

00:13:57.914 --> 00:13:59.571
He is trying to drop Wepner.

00:13:59.571 --> 00:14:00.851
There's a good combination!

00:14:00.851 --> 00:14:02.372
Wepner's ready to go!

00:14:02.372 --> 00:14:03.262
He's ready to go!

00:14:03.262 --> 00:14:04.315
Ali goes on!

00:14:04.315 --> 00:14:05.639
Wepner is staggering!

00:14:05.639 --> 00:14:07.459
He's out of his face right now!

00:14:07.459 --> 00:14:08.768
And the combination!

00:14:08.768 --> 00:14:10.480
Ali has this man in trouble!

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:13.011
Wepner, attempting to hang on!

00:14:13.011 --> 00:14:14.149
He's trying to hang on!

00:14:14.149 --> 00:14:15.899
He's off on his feet!

00:14:17.439 --> 00:14:19.856
A right hand off a left hook!

00:14:22.806 --> 00:14:26.223
Four, it's up to five, six, seven, eight!

00:14:28.115 --> 00:14:30.643
The referee stops the fight!

00:14:30.643 --> 00:14:32.536
- And it's really silly, when
you think about fightin'.

00:14:32.536 --> 00:14:35.403
I look at other fighters fight,
and I say, I must be a fool.

00:14:35.403 --> 00:14:36.866
Here are two men, like two roosters,

00:14:36.866 --> 00:14:38.155
you all know them cockfights.

00:14:38.155 --> 00:14:40.050
They take two roosters,
and they put 'em out,

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:41.156
and they put knives on 'em,

00:14:41.156 --> 00:14:43.034
and the roosters are fightin' each other,

00:14:43.034 --> 00:14:45.544
and they're not even mad,
don't know each other.

00:14:45.544 --> 00:14:47.605
And just to please somebody!

00:14:47.605 --> 00:14:48.742
And here are two men in the ring,

00:14:48.742 --> 00:14:51.041
fightin' each other, and
they're hittin' each other,

00:14:51.041 --> 00:14:52.852
(grunts) and they bleed,
and they're fightin'!

00:14:52.852 --> 00:14:54.068
What they mad about?

00:14:54.068 --> 00:14:55.562
They're not mad about nothin'!

00:14:55.562 --> 00:14:58.620
Just a bunch of agitatin',
bloodthirsty people,

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:00.312
sayin' you can whoop
him, he can whoop him,

00:15:00.312 --> 00:15:01.380
my man can whoop your man.

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:02.782
Alright, you all get in there and fight!

00:15:02.782 --> 00:15:04.633
Humans should have more sense than that.

00:15:04.633 --> 00:15:05.835
And you're sittin' out there, dressed up,

00:15:05.835 --> 00:15:08.093
drinkin' your beer, and... (fake laughs)

00:15:08.093 --> 00:15:08.949
(audience laughing)

00:15:08.949 --> 00:15:11.900
And they just fightin',
and just... (grunts)

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:13.134
And this is serious!

00:15:13.134 --> 00:15:16.071
The nose'll bleed, and the
eyes cut, the teeth is out.

00:15:16.071 --> 00:15:18.242
And the brain, they
might have a concussion.

00:15:18.242 --> 00:15:20.651
Just to please you human beings!

00:15:20.651 --> 00:15:21.551
It's real savage.

00:15:21.551 --> 00:15:23.233
And I said, I'm not gon'
be that kind of fighter.

00:15:23.233 --> 00:15:24.768
I'm going to dance, and be pretty.

00:15:24.768 --> 00:15:26.203
I'm just gon' win on points.

00:15:26.203 --> 00:15:28.043
And if I hurt my man,
I'm going to let him go.

00:15:28.043 --> 00:15:30.423
I'm not going to kill him, just
because somebody's watchin'.

00:15:30.423 --> 00:15:32.063
I did it to Floyd Patterson.

00:15:32.063 --> 00:15:33.715
I did it to George Chuvalo.

00:15:33.715 --> 00:15:35.465
I did it to Karl Mildenberger.

00:15:35.465 --> 00:15:37.219
I did it to Henry Cooper,
when he started bleedin'.

00:15:37.219 --> 00:15:39.099
I pulled off of him, deliberately,

00:15:39.099 --> 00:15:40.852
blood just pumpin' and gushin'!

00:15:40.852 --> 00:15:42.030
And he's got a family.

00:15:42.030 --> 00:15:42.863
He's got children.

00:15:42.863 --> 00:15:44.915
And I just can't, James Ellis.

00:15:44.915 --> 00:15:47.473
I can't see myself with
a man on the ropes,

00:15:47.473 --> 00:15:49.894
and just to prove how bad
I am, and I see I got him!

00:15:49.894 --> 00:15:51.588
His eye's in his head, he's helpless,

00:15:51.588 --> 00:15:53.906
and I'm just deliberately hittin' him!

00:15:53.906 --> 00:15:54.928
I don't do that.

00:15:54.928 --> 00:15:58.011
(upbeat funky music)

00:16:02.324 --> 00:16:05.407
- [Announcer] 1:30 left in the fight!

00:16:07.873 --> 00:16:09.760
(audience roaring)

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:11.072
That left!

00:16:11.072 --> 00:16:13.321
What a, it came from nowhere!

00:16:13.321 --> 00:16:15.623
Ali came through with a left!

00:16:15.623 --> 00:16:16.972
The crowd's screaming!

00:16:16.972 --> 00:16:18.589
The first knockdown of the fight!

00:16:18.589 --> 00:16:20.139
He took the man to eight!

00:16:20.139 --> 00:16:23.556
And now, Ali is behaving like the old Ali!

00:16:23.556 --> 00:16:25.619
One more knockdown in this round,

00:16:25.619 --> 00:16:28.315
the fight is automatically over!

00:16:28.315 --> 00:16:30.342
Bonavena is running!

00:16:30.342 --> 00:16:32.559
If he goes down again, it's over!

00:16:32.559 --> 00:16:34.570
Ali is the knockout winner!

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:37.159
At two minutes and three seconds!

00:16:37.159 --> 00:16:40.291
By my unofficial clock,
of the final round,

00:16:40.291 --> 00:16:41.846
it's again with the left!

00:16:41.846 --> 00:16:44.746
I'm going up to ring center!

00:16:44.746 --> 00:16:48.052
- Whether it's a world champion
boxer, a basketball player,

00:16:48.052 --> 00:16:51.447
a track star, a horse, even animals,

00:16:51.447 --> 00:16:55.111
I find out that this Mark
Spitz, for an example,

00:16:55.111 --> 00:16:57.241
he's a world champion.

00:16:57.241 --> 00:16:59.621
But, what made him the world champion,

00:16:59.621 --> 00:17:02.491
was that he seemed to, at the right time,

00:17:02.491 --> 00:17:05.852
when the pressure's down,
at the last few yards,

00:17:05.852 --> 00:17:09.771
he can get that lead, or he's
got enough left to make it.

00:17:09.771 --> 00:17:11.530
I fought Ken Norton.

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:14.748
My last fight, the fight was
even, up until the last round.

00:17:14.748 --> 00:17:16.536
But, I had somethin' that he didn't have,

00:17:16.536 --> 00:17:17.944
although I'm much older.

00:17:17.944 --> 00:17:20.338
And that was the last minute kick.

00:17:20.338 --> 00:17:21.287
- [Interviewer] What's
that last minute kick?

00:17:21.287 --> 00:17:22.901
Is that something--
- Just the stamina,

00:17:22.901 --> 00:17:23.920
the strength.

00:17:23.920 --> 00:17:24.892
- [Interviewer] It's more than training.

00:17:24.892 --> 00:17:27.989
- The mental capacity to
realize what's involved

00:17:27.989 --> 00:17:29.440
and how important it is,

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:30.599
and make it about to do somethin'

00:17:30.599 --> 00:17:31.861
that's really too tired to do.

00:17:31.861 --> 00:17:33.474
Your mind makes you do it.

00:17:33.474 --> 00:17:36.342
Mark Spitz, this Olympic
track star I was mentionin',

00:17:36.342 --> 00:17:38.000
he wasn't that much greater

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:39.320
than all the people in the world.

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:42.031
But, sometimes, he won by just that much.

00:17:42.031 --> 00:17:45.135
And the champion is just one

00:17:45.135 --> 00:17:47.804
who can come out at the last
minute and close the show.

00:17:47.804 --> 00:17:49.720
As they say, the star closes the show.

00:17:49.720 --> 00:17:52.576
A 14, 15 round fight, and it's even,

00:17:52.576 --> 00:17:55.699
and usually, this champion,
you can depend on him

00:17:55.699 --> 00:17:57.281
to come through at the last two seconds,

00:17:57.281 --> 00:17:59.730
and find some initiative from somewhere.

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:00.909
- [Interviewer] Is it discipline?

00:18:00.909 --> 00:18:03.382
- Not only that, it's mental and physical.

00:18:03.382 --> 00:18:05.776
His body's in physical shape to do it.

00:18:05.776 --> 00:18:08.187
Plus, mentally too.

00:18:08.187 --> 00:18:10.083
He's got his self in condition,

00:18:10.083 --> 00:18:12.324
where both fellas may be, sometimes,

00:18:12.324 --> 00:18:14.303
the wheel can outdo the skill.

00:18:14.303 --> 00:18:16.489
And sometimes, the
fella's will is stronger

00:18:16.489 --> 00:18:18.709
than the man who's
actually better physically.

00:18:18.709 --> 00:18:21.812
And the determination
weakens the other man,

00:18:21.812 --> 00:18:23.403
just to see him so determined.

00:18:23.403 --> 00:18:26.486
(upbeat funky music)

00:18:33.872 --> 00:18:36.176
- [Announcer] Ali's moving in on London!

00:18:36.176 --> 00:18:39.314
A huge line of punches by Muhammad Ali!

00:18:39.314 --> 00:18:41.494
London goes down!

00:18:41.494 --> 00:18:45.243
The referee sends Ali to a neutral corner!

00:18:45.243 --> 00:18:48.052
- Your pre-fight build ups

00:18:48.052 --> 00:18:49.292
and when you go to the weigh-in,

00:18:49.292 --> 00:18:51.808
and you have, they appear,

00:18:51.808 --> 00:18:53.840
mock-up battles with the other opponent.

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:54.757
Are they really?

00:18:54.757 --> 00:18:56.475
How much is that is towards the--

00:18:56.475 --> 00:18:58.168
- Well, I'm not really
wantin' to fight them,

00:18:58.168 --> 00:19:00.132
because I wouldn't be paid.

00:19:00.132 --> 00:19:01.862
But, I really do be angry!

00:19:01.862 --> 00:19:03.200
I have to psych myself up.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:04.393
I put myself on spots.

00:19:04.393 --> 00:19:05.481
I say...

00:19:05.481 --> 00:19:06.314
- [Man] It's just for press,

00:19:06.314 --> 00:19:07.561
for the build up for the fight?

00:19:07.561 --> 00:19:09.716
- Well, not really,
because even in the fight

00:19:09.716 --> 00:19:10.549
is when that happens.

00:19:10.549 --> 00:19:12.885
And it's really sold out by them.

00:19:12.885 --> 00:19:14.348
But, it actually puts
fear into your opponent,

00:19:14.348 --> 00:19:16.136
like George Foreman.

00:19:16.136 --> 00:19:17.944
Just before the fight, I'm lookin' at him

00:19:17.944 --> 00:19:19.526
when the man's givin' us instructions.

00:19:19.526 --> 00:19:22.864
I said, sucka, you are in trouble tonight!

00:19:22.864 --> 00:19:26.123
You are fightin' the greatest
fighter for all times!

00:19:26.123 --> 00:19:27.534
You heard I was the greatest,

00:19:27.534 --> 00:19:28.712
like you just said you heard this.

00:19:28.712 --> 00:19:29.714
Now, you see it!

00:19:29.714 --> 00:19:31.354
I said, you said I was the greatest!

00:19:31.354 --> 00:19:33.992
But, you're going to see, I'm fast, sucka!

00:19:33.992 --> 00:19:35.551
I'm going to burn you up!

00:19:35.551 --> 00:19:36.912
You're fightin' your idol!

00:19:36.912 --> 00:19:39.022
When you were a little
kid, you heard about me!

00:19:39.022 --> 00:19:40.998
You know, and he was,
he wasn't even fightin'.

00:19:40.998 --> 00:19:42.987
He didn't have his first fight until 1969.

00:19:42.987 --> 00:19:45.657
I'd been in exile two
years after all I'd done!

00:19:45.657 --> 00:19:46.879
He just started fightin'!

00:19:46.879 --> 00:19:49.546
So, and when I was fightin'
people like you in the 60s,

00:19:49.546 --> 00:19:51.235
he was just a little kid
in junior high school!

00:19:51.235 --> 00:19:54.007
I said, you're meetin'
your master, your idol.

00:19:54.007 --> 00:19:56.045
He looked at me!

00:19:56.045 --> 00:19:57.972
And then, I went back, first round.

00:19:57.972 --> 00:19:59.432
I laid in the corners, right?

00:19:59.432 --> 00:20:00.944
I said, come on, show me somethin'!

00:20:00.944 --> 00:20:02.123
I talked through the whole fight.

00:20:02.123 --> 00:20:03.324
I don't know if you all knew it.

00:20:03.324 --> 00:20:04.587
I talked through the whole fight.

00:20:04.587 --> 00:20:06.302
I said, come on, sucka!

00:20:06.302 --> 00:20:07.864
I said, show me somethin'!

00:20:07.864 --> 00:20:09.434
They told me you could hit hard!

00:20:09.434 --> 00:20:10.792
You're just a sissy!
(audience laughing)

00:20:10.792 --> 00:20:12.040
Come on, sucka!

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:13.720
Show me somethin'!

00:20:13.720 --> 00:20:16.022
Come on, you can do
better than that, George!

00:20:16.022 --> 00:20:17.311
You want to carton me around?

00:20:17.311 --> 00:20:18.617
You waitin' to carton me?

00:20:18.617 --> 00:20:20.344
And he just... (grunts)

00:20:20.344 --> 00:20:23.101
And then, once in a while,
I just go... (exhales)

00:20:23.101 --> 00:20:25.913
You see, the quickest way to
a point, is a straight line.

00:20:25.913 --> 00:20:27.736
To hit me, he had to do that.

00:20:27.736 --> 00:20:29.727
(Ali grunting)

00:20:29.727 --> 00:20:32.185
And while he's doing' that, I said...

00:20:32.185 --> 00:20:33.796
I'm taggin' him with jabs, right?

00:20:33.796 --> 00:20:34.629
Pop, pop!

00:20:34.629 --> 00:20:35.555
You're a fighter, you know.

00:20:35.555 --> 00:20:37.477
When you ever meet a man,
comin' at ya like that,

00:20:37.477 --> 00:20:38.368
don't worry about it.

00:20:38.368 --> 00:20:40.336
Don't duck like it's so powerful.

00:20:40.336 --> 00:20:41.795
Just pop him, pop!

00:20:41.795 --> 00:20:43.441
See, see, he's goin'...

00:20:43.441 --> 00:20:44.726
I'da hit him, before he got there.

00:20:44.726 --> 00:20:47.726
(audience laughing)

00:20:50.015 --> 00:20:51.753
He's just takin' one hit!

00:20:51.753 --> 00:20:53.030
- [Dickie] What else
did you say to him, Ali?

00:20:53.030 --> 00:20:53.863
What else did you say to him?

00:20:53.863 --> 00:20:56.516
- Oh, I grabbed his head
sometimes, and I said,

00:20:56.516 --> 00:20:58.287
look at you, look at you!

00:20:58.287 --> 00:21:01.183
Round seven and you're tired!

00:21:01.183 --> 00:21:03.203
You have eight more rounds to go!

00:21:03.203 --> 00:21:04.405
Come on, keep punchin'!

00:21:04.405 --> 00:21:05.795
I want ya to get tired!

00:21:05.795 --> 00:21:07.104
I said, uh oh.

00:21:07.104 --> 00:21:09.805
I said, this is the
wrong place to get tired!

00:21:09.805 --> 00:21:12.007
This is the wrong place to get tired!

00:21:12.007 --> 00:21:13.086
And he just throwin' 'em!

00:21:13.086 --> 00:21:14.935
I said, then, he got a
couple bruises, his nose,

00:21:14.935 --> 00:21:16.340
his face is kind of swollen.

00:21:16.340 --> 00:21:17.219
I said, look at ya!

00:21:17.219 --> 00:21:19.271
You're the world heavyweight champion!

00:21:19.271 --> 00:21:21.419
You're the world, wop,
I was hittin' him, wop!

00:21:21.419 --> 00:21:23.547
You're the world heavyweight champion!

00:21:23.547 --> 00:21:25.770
And look at me, you can't, pop, I hit ya!

00:21:25.770 --> 00:21:27.291
Just, watch, here come another one, pop!

00:21:27.291 --> 00:21:28.411
I said, looka there, looka there!

00:21:28.411 --> 00:21:29.244
He threw one at me.

00:21:29.244 --> 00:21:30.077
I said, come on, come on, get me!

00:21:30.077 --> 00:21:31.252
I'm going back to the rope now.

00:21:31.252 --> 00:21:32.085
I laid back.

00:21:32.085 --> 00:21:33.052
I said, okay, take your best shot!

00:21:33.052 --> 00:21:33.891
Take your best shot!

00:21:33.891 --> 00:21:36.590
(Ali panting)
(audience laughing)

00:21:36.590 --> 00:21:37.423
He's breathin'!

00:21:37.423 --> 00:21:39.153
I said, aw, aw, you finished boy!

00:21:39.153 --> 00:21:41.051
You are in trouble!

00:21:41.051 --> 00:21:44.580
I said, you don't have, but
two chances, slim and none!

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:45.579
You in trouble!

00:21:45.579 --> 00:21:47.259
I talked to him through the whole fight.

00:21:47.259 --> 00:21:50.342
(upbeat funky music)

00:22:03.292 --> 00:22:06.209
(audience roaring)

00:22:19.010 --> 00:22:22.432
- I was told that it's a
big honor to be invited

00:22:22.432 --> 00:22:24.702
to speak at a place like Harvard.

00:22:24.702 --> 00:22:27.702
(audience laughing)

00:22:35.528 --> 00:22:36.930
I'm trying to be serious,

00:22:36.930 --> 00:22:38.471
but you want to make me laugh anyway!

00:22:38.471 --> 00:22:41.471
(audience laughing)

00:22:43.940 --> 00:22:47.359
I understand that out of
people, such as you all,

00:22:47.359 --> 00:22:50.520
come presidents, and
governors, and mayors,

00:22:50.520 --> 00:22:53.222
and great doctors, and
physicians, and scientists,

00:22:53.222 --> 00:22:55.030
and everything.

00:22:55.030 --> 00:22:57.721
So, I say, well to get somethin' together,

00:22:57.721 --> 00:23:01.180
to talk to these people,
it's got to be pretty heavy.

00:23:01.180 --> 00:23:04.180
(audience laughing)

00:23:05.618 --> 00:23:08.321
If you had told I'd be
offered a professorship

00:23:08.321 --> 00:23:11.751
to teach philosophy, and poetry at Oxford,

00:23:11.751 --> 00:23:13.861
and speakin' at Harvard.

00:23:13.861 --> 00:23:15.022
Man, I never would've believed it.

00:23:15.022 --> 00:23:18.529
So, I'm really humble, and I'm thankful,

00:23:18.529 --> 00:23:22.830
to be here at such a
high seat of learnin'.

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:24.145
And now, I'm just a boxer.

00:23:24.145 --> 00:23:26.066
But, most boxers can't even talk.

00:23:26.066 --> 00:23:29.468
(audience laughing)

00:23:29.468 --> 00:23:32.376
You couldn't invite Joe
Frazier or George Foreman!

00:23:32.376 --> 00:23:35.376
(audience cheering)

00:23:43.720 --> 00:23:47.887
This is the Ali Shuffle!
(audience cheering)

00:23:52.659 --> 00:23:53.659
This here...

00:24:06.457 --> 00:24:08.047
- [Reporter] In a long
and glorious history

00:24:08.047 --> 00:24:09.710
of Harvard University,

00:24:09.710 --> 00:24:14.082
no speaker ever receives such
a tumultuous standing ovation!

00:24:14.082 --> 00:24:17.165
(upbeat funky music)

00:24:21.991 --> 00:24:23.770
- [Announcer] Very even fight.

00:24:23.770 --> 00:24:25.853
Ali, a sneaky right hand!

00:24:26.803 --> 00:24:28.542
Another sneaky right hand!

00:24:28.542 --> 00:24:29.542
This time...

00:24:31.621 --> 00:24:34.538
(audience roaring)

00:24:37.223 --> 00:24:39.723
Three, four, five, six, seven,

00:24:42.014 --> 00:24:44.601
Foreman, just stumbling
to his knees, eight!

00:24:44.601 --> 00:24:45.713
That's it!

00:24:45.713 --> 00:24:47.057
The fight is done!

00:24:47.057 --> 00:24:50.474
Muhammad Ali, tonight, instant knockdown!

00:24:53.571 --> 00:24:54.988
George Foreman...

00:24:57.387 --> 00:24:58.568
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:24:58.568 --> 00:25:01.947
I made this video, because
Lex Vendenherich asked me to.

00:25:01.947 --> 00:25:03.227
So, if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:25:03.227 --> 00:25:05.346
that you want me to profile next,

00:25:05.346 --> 00:25:06.605
leave it in the comments below,

00:25:06.605 --> 00:25:08.025
and I'll see what I can do.

00:25:08.025 --> 00:25:10.077
I'd also love to know
which of Muhammad Ali's

00:25:10.077 --> 00:25:12.489
Top Ten Rules meant the most to you.

00:25:12.489 --> 00:25:14.677
Leave it in the comments and
I'll join the discussion.

00:25:14.677 --> 00:25:16.038
Thank you so much for watching.

00:25:16.038 --> 00:25:19.538
Continue to believe and I'll see you soon.

00:25:24.589 --> 00:25:26.136
- Did you ever get
frightened before a fight?

00:25:26.136 --> 00:25:27.285
You ever get nervous before a fight?

00:25:27.285 --> 00:25:28.626
- I'm nervous, but not frightened.

00:25:28.626 --> 00:25:32.797
I'm nervous, because I
have a great insight on,

00:25:32.797 --> 00:25:35.888
I just don't see the
audience, every camera.

00:25:35.888 --> 00:25:37.035
I see millions of people.

00:25:37.035 --> 00:25:38.318
Like, the Frazier fight was watched

00:25:38.318 --> 00:25:40.538
by ten hundred million people,

00:25:40.538 --> 00:25:42.576
which is five times the
population of everybody

00:25:42.576 --> 00:25:44.065
in the United States.

00:25:44.065 --> 00:25:47.182
Just to picture a arena
with one million people.

00:25:47.182 --> 00:25:48.924
I imagine you couldn't see 'em all.

00:25:48.924 --> 00:25:51.231
And just think about a hundred million,

00:25:51.231 --> 00:25:53.280
and ten hundred million.

00:25:53.280 --> 00:25:54.932
And all those people, and everything,

00:25:54.932 --> 00:25:55.994
and that makes me nervous.

00:25:55.994 --> 00:25:56.833
Just the idea of me,

00:25:56.833 --> 00:25:59.114
just bein' a humble fella from Kentucky.

00:25:59.114 --> 00:26:00.781
Got lucky in sports.

00:26:01.892 --> 00:26:04.942
And now, here's the
house, the famous Pipeton.

00:26:04.942 --> 00:26:07.711
A place like Thailand,
to the government house,

00:26:07.711 --> 00:26:10.103
and Arabian, the government
officials took time off

00:26:10.103 --> 00:26:10.936
to watch the fight.

00:26:10.936 --> 00:26:13.154
And just for two men boxing,

00:26:13.154 --> 00:26:16.175
attracting so many people of
all races, and nationalities,

00:26:16.175 --> 00:26:17.917
and Hawaii, you understand,

00:26:17.917 --> 00:26:20.787
they stopped, closing all of
the factories, and the people,

00:26:20.787 --> 00:26:22.709
they set televisions on
every other street corner.

00:26:22.709 --> 00:26:25.367
People came out, watchin'
the fight on the streets.

00:26:25.367 --> 00:26:28.216
And every bar in America, every house,

00:26:28.216 --> 00:26:31.106
even traffic was still during that fight.

00:26:31.106 --> 00:26:32.267
And Madison Square Garden,

00:26:32.267 --> 00:26:33.915
ten thousand people couldn't get in,

00:26:33.915 --> 00:26:35.125
and just over one man.

00:26:35.125 --> 00:26:37.268
And just imagine all
them people watching you.

00:26:37.268 --> 00:26:40.698
That makes me nervous,
until I get started.

00:26:40.698 --> 00:26:41.888
- [Michael] And then, no nerves at all?

00:26:41.888 --> 00:26:42.721
- No.

00:26:42.721 --> 00:26:44.442
- How about this villain, though?

00:26:44.442 --> 00:26:46.532
You're getting to be the villain
and Liston is getting be--

00:26:46.532 --> 00:26:47.763
- Yeah, at first, Liston was the villain

00:26:47.763 --> 00:26:48.596
and didn't know about it.

00:26:48.596 --> 00:26:50.822
Like Liston, Liston was a
thug, Liston was a gangster,

00:26:50.822 --> 00:26:52.453
Liston was this, Liston was that,

00:26:52.453 --> 00:26:53.759
everybody wants to see Liston beat!

00:26:53.759 --> 00:26:56.029
And now, all of a sudden,
Liston is the savior!

00:26:56.029 --> 00:26:57.097
- You know, I get--

00:26:57.097 --> 00:26:57.930
- Actually, I like it!

00:26:57.930 --> 00:26:59.358
That makes me rumble!

00:26:59.358 --> 00:27:00.354
Don't we rumble?

00:27:00.354 --> 00:27:03.082
- [Group] Float like a
butterfly and sting like a bee!

00:27:03.082 --> 00:27:06.632
(exclaims) Rumble, young man, rumble!

00:27:06.632 --> 00:27:08.606
- (exclaims) That's what we going to do!

00:27:08.606 --> 00:27:09.836
We're going to rumble!

00:27:09.836 --> 00:27:11.402
Well, I have a poem.

00:27:11.402 --> 00:27:13.017
(audience laughing)
We got one minute?

00:27:13.017 --> 00:27:14.497
The poem goes like this.

00:27:14.497 --> 00:27:15.368
People said, what's going to happen,

00:27:15.368 --> 00:27:16.547
when you meet Joe Frazier again?

00:27:16.547 --> 00:27:18.468
Here's how the fight's
going to sound on the radio,

00:27:18.468 --> 00:27:20.018
for those of you who can't afford to buy

00:27:20.018 --> 00:27:21.928
the expensive theater seats.

00:27:21.928 --> 00:27:23.704
And the fight goes like this.

00:27:23.704 --> 00:27:25.826
Ding, Ali comes out to meet Frazier,

00:27:25.826 --> 00:27:27.698
but Frazier starts to retreat!

00:27:27.698 --> 00:27:29.469
If Frazier goes back on his father,

00:27:29.469 --> 00:27:31.718
he'll wind up in a ringside seat!

00:27:31.718 --> 00:27:32.725
Ali swings with a left!

00:27:32.725 --> 00:27:34.087
Ali swings with with a right!

00:27:34.087 --> 00:27:35.879
Look at the kid carry the fight!

00:27:35.879 --> 00:27:38.578
Frazier keeps backin', but
there's not enough room!

00:27:38.578 --> 00:27:39.548
It's a matter of time!

00:27:39.548 --> 00:27:41.356
There, Ali lowers the boom!

00:27:41.356 --> 00:27:42.819
Now, Ali lands with a right!

00:27:42.819 --> 00:27:44.642
What a beautiful swing!

00:27:44.642 --> 00:27:47.672
And the punch-less Frazier,
clean out of the ring!

00:27:47.672 --> 00:27:51.755
(audience laughing and cheering)

00:27:52.894 --> 00:27:53.727
Frazier.

00:27:58.495 --> 00:28:01.026
Frazier's still risin'.

00:28:01.026 --> 00:28:03.296
But, the referee wears a frown.

00:28:03.296 --> 00:28:05.958
For, he can't start counting
'til Frazier comes down.

00:28:05.958 --> 00:28:08.958
(audience laughing)

00:28:10.134 --> 00:28:12.987
Now, Frazier disappears from view!

00:28:12.987 --> 00:28:15.066
The crowd is gettin' frantic!

00:28:15.066 --> 00:28:17.507
But, our radar stations
have picked him up!

00:28:17.507 --> 00:28:19.460
He's somewhere over the Atlantic!

00:28:19.460 --> 00:28:21.059
(audience laughing)

00:28:21.059 --> 00:28:23.390
Who would have thought,
when they came to the fight,

00:28:23.390 --> 00:28:24.757
that they would've witnessed the launchin'

00:28:24.757 --> 00:28:26.226
of a colored satellite!

00:28:26.226 --> 00:28:30.309
(audience laughing and cheering)

